ifficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. We can argue that A's quick decision-making and attention are vital, and his concern for others may mitigate communication issues. However, his egocentric nature and lack of willingness to further education raise concerns about adaptability and teamwork.\n\nWe could also bring up D's responsibility and problem solving, but moody and loner.\n\nI think a balanced approach: I will acknowledge B's strengths but raise concerns about his communication and memory, and propose that Candidate A's quick decision-making and excellent attention may be more critical, and his concern for others suggests better crew cooperation, though his communication difficulty and egocentric traits are concerns. I will vote for Candidate A, but note need to discuss others.\n\nThus public message: state vote Candidate A, reference Agent 2's points, bring own facts, explain why A may be better.\n\nProceed."}
